# Headers for the files served without the Worker (it sets its own: see src/server.ts), and for the wiki's clips,
# which it serves with byte ranges and these headers. Most are named by a hash of their contents, so they never
# change: play/v/HASH/ by scripts/web --package, assets/ by Vite and wiki/og/NAME.HASH.png by src/wiki/build/og.ts
# (HASH its bytes'). The wiki's media (wiki/media, docs/wiki-media.md) keep their names when they're rendered
# again, so they're cached for a day: a clip a pull request re-renders reaches a reader who has the old one
# within a day, and a URL a search engine or another site has stays the same.
#
# Every file gets the headers the Worker gives what it serves (src/server.ts's EVERY_RESPONSE, which
# test-server.mjs checks these against; docs/web-deploy.md, "HTTPS" and "Security headers"). A header two rules
# give is joined with a comma, so no other rule gives one of them.
/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'self'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: autoplay=(self), fullscreen=(self), gamepad=(self), camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=(), midi=(), display-capture=()
/play/v/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
# The game's assets, assets/bundle.bin (about 1.2 MiB, a fifth of that compressed) and assets/config/bundle.bin,
# which it fetches as it starts. The asset store serves .bin as application/octet-stream, a type Cloudflare doesn't compress, so they'd
# go over the wire whole: Protobuf's is a binary type it does compress, with gzip or Brotli as the browser asks.
# The game reads the bytes, whatever the type (crates/app/src/web.rs's fetch), and nothing else asks for them.
/play/v/*.bin
  Content-Type: application/x-protobuf
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/wiki/media/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400
# The media's LICENSE.txt and NOTICE.txt (scripts/wiki-media), in UTF-8. The asset store serves
# .txt as text/plain without a charset, which a browser decodes by guessing, often as windows-1252, and they skip
# the Worker, which adds it to the other .txt files (src/server.ts). A Content-Type here replaces the store's.
/wiki/media/*.txt
  Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
# The landing page's media and the logo every page shows (public/media/), which keep their names: a day, as the
# wiki's media. Its pictures skip the Worker, and its video comes through it for byte ranges (src/server.ts), with
# these headers.
/media/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
/wiki/og/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
